#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Local hot-swapping Anthropic proxy: rotate OAuth tokens by live quota.

Point Claude Code at it and it never has to restart to change tokens:

    claude-token-proxy &                 # starts on 127.0.0.1:8788
    ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788 claude

Per request the proxy injects the `Authorization: Bearer` of the token with the
most weekly headroom (read live from `anthropic-ratelimit-unified-7d-utilization`
response headers), skips tokens in 429 cooldown, and on a 429/401/403/529 from
upstream transparently retries the SAME request with the next-best token. So a
long-lived `claude` session rolls over to a fresh token mid-stream with no restart
— the same idea as KarpelesLab/teamclaude, reusing the selection logic from
claude-token-refresh, dependency-free (Python stdlib only).

Tokens are read from ~/cctoken (lines containing sk-ant-oat... tokens); the file is
re-read when its mtime changes, so adding or replacing a token needs no restart.
A token that authenticates badly (401/403) is parked, then re-probed periodically,
so a re-login heals the pool on its own. Comment lines are ignored, so you can
label each token with its account email.

Token values are never logged; rows are identified by a short SHA-256 fingerprint.

`GET /_status` returns the live pool as JSON (fingerprints, utilization, validity,
retry cooldowns, quota status, and local response counters) without touching upstream.
`GET /_usage` is the same redacted per-token view intended for Waybar and scripts.
The proxy refreshes the read-only `/api/oauth/usage` endpoint every five minutes;
OAuth scope failures are reported per token and never invalidate inference.

Cross-provider quota oracle (docs/research/generic-llm-proxy.md, option c): on the
same five-minute cadence the proxy polls the ChatGPT/Codex `wham/usage` and
DeepSeek `/user/balance` endpoints with the credentials pi already holds in
`~/.pi/agent/auth.json` (read-only; OAuth is never refreshed, `!cmd` keys are never
executed, tokens are never logged) and exposes them under `providers` in `/_usage`.
`GET /_route?model=<claude-model>` ranks substitutes across providers from the
equivalence table `config/llm-proxy/routes.json` (`CC_PROXY_ROUTES` overrides the
path; re-read on mtime change) — Anthropic pool first via the read-only pick
preview, then the table order — and says which is routable and why not. It is a
pure read: nothing is forwarded to another provider by this proxy unless the
DeepSeek passthrough below is switched on.
Readings from undocumented endpoints degrade to `unavailable`, never to 0 %.

DeepSeek Anthropic-passthrough (opt-in, decision 4 in the same doc): with
`CC_PROXY_DEEPSEEK_FALLBACK=1`, a Messages request that NO OAuth token can serve
(`pick()` returns None: every account parked, cooling or forced down — never on
mere pressure or threshold) is forwarded unchanged to DeepSeek's Anthropic-compatible
endpoint `https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic` with `x-api-key` from the DeepSeek
credential pi holds and the model rewritten per the `deepseek` entry of
`routes.json`. Gates: the cached balance must be above
`CC_PROXY_DEEPSEEK_MIN_BALANCE` and `is_available` must not be false, and the
model must have a `deepseek` route; otherwise the usual "no OAuth account can
serve" error is returned. The OAuth bearer is never sent to DeepSeek, a DeepSeek
error (e.g. 402 on a negative balance) is returned to the client as-is and never
retried against Anthropic, and every fallback request is logged and counted
(`routing.fallback` in `/_usage`). This changes who is billed and who receives the
conversation, which is why it is off by default.

Env knobs: CC_PROXY_PORT, CCTOKEN_FILE, CC_PROXY_THRESHOLD (default 0.98),
CC_PROXY_SEED (1/0), CC_PROXY_MIN_VALID (default 2, warn below this),
CC_PROXY_WATCH_INTERVAL (default 30s), CC_PROXY_REVALIDATE_INTERVAL (default 600s).
Token selection (see docs/research/claude-token-rotation-oss.md): CC_PROXY_PICK
(`pressure` default — spend perishable weekly quota first, model-aware bucket;
`headroom` — legacy lowest-7d-utilization) and CC_PROXY_PICK_TOLERANCE (default
1.5 — stickiness band that keeps the previous token, and its prompt cache,
unless another token's pressure is this many times better). Pressure is
`min(7d headroom / seconds to 7d reset, 5h headroom / seconds to 5h reset)`;
unknown utilization/reset means full headroom and a full window. Threshold preference
applies to both the model's weekly bucket and the 5h bucket.
429 pacing: CC_PROXY_BURST_WAIT_MAX (default 15s) — a 429 that does not mark a
spent bucket is a per-minute burst limit, so the proxy waits out Retry-After (up
to this cap) and retries the SAME token once instead of rotating; rotating would
only move the burst to another account and throw away the warm prompt cache.
A quota-429 (`anthropic-ratelimit-unified*-status: rejected`) still cools the
token down and fails over immediately.
A control file $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cc-proxy/force_cooldown may list fingerprints
(whitespace-separated) to treat as cooled-down — used for testing rollover without
burning real quota.
Oracle knobs: CC_PROXY_ROUTES (routes.json path), CC_PROXY_DEEPSEEK_MIN_BALANCE
(default 1.0 — DeepSeek is only routable above this balance), PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR
(where auth.json lives), DEEPSEEK_ACCOUNT_LABEL (display label for the key),
CC_PROXY_DEEPSEEK_FALLBACK (default 0; 1 enables the passthrough above).
"""

